# Specification authoring rules — Analisador de desempenho futebol

- Specs are **technology-agnostic**: describe WHAT and WHY, never HOW. No frameworks, SDKs, databases, queues, caching, or protocols in `spec.md`.
- User stories use **As a / I want / So that**; acceptance scenarios use Gherkin (`Scenario`, `Given`, `When`, `Then`, `And`) with observable, business-readable outcomes.
- Functional requirements must be testable; success criteria must be measurable and technology-agnostic.
- Test scenarios follow the ID convention `TS-USNN-NNN` (per user story), `TS-EC-NNN` (edge cases), `TS-NFR-NNN` (non-functional), and map back to FR/NFR ids.
- Prefer generating/regenerating spec artifacts via **`/specforge.*`** commands or MCP `sdd_*` tools over hand-editing.
- NEVER modify shared references in `.specforge/templates/` or `.specforge/shared/` — they are read-only.
